    "Notes Updated": "10/2/2024",
    "Scouting Notes": "Definitely concerned about how 2024 went.\n Not impacting the ball\n Can't stay healthy\n Worry about too many swing changes/adjustements\n Defense is still really good, and he's still an elite athlete so I'm leaving him near my top 30 for now.\n Need to see the bat step back up in 2025",
    "Notes Updated 2": "7/18/2022",
    "Scouting Notes 2": "2022 Draft Report'\n  Personal favorite of mine in this draft. Really excited that the Brewers got him.\n  Believe he was ranked far too low. Upper first round talent.\n  Weird setup and load seemed to turn people off, but I don't care about that. He's consistently on time. \n  The high hands actually seem to help his bat path.\n  Combination of bat to ball, with his bat speed is not seen anywhere else in this class.\n  Extremely low chase rate (9%) and whiff rate.\n  In game power has not shown up yet. However, OVER 60% of his batted balls were hit > 95 mph. \n  Along with the exit velos over 95 MPH, he has been up to 113 MPH. He has raw power that he can tap into.\n  If I had a nitpick, I think he takes some hittable pitches, because he's so patient. \n  The over abundance of patience is probably fine, because he does not panic when behind in counts and doesn't need to \"\"shorten up\"\" to avoid striking out.\n  Above average speed, but uses the Brian Roberts stealing technique to a lot of success.\n  I bet he will be able to steal double digits in the majors pretty easily, possibly getting to 30+ bases with the likelihood of new rules helping baserunners.\n  Defensive actions at short are really good. Glove will stick and could be close to plus.\n  Arm strength is a bit of a concern from pundits, but he does a great job of getting his throws off quickly and personally I think there's plenty of zip, I grade it as an above average arm. The quickness of the release should alleviate a lot of that concern anyway though.\n  If he has to move off of short to play second, he's likely a 70 grade defender.\n  Have a feeling I will be the high guy on Brown for a while. I would've been happy with taking him in the early teens of this draft.The fact they were able to get him so far below slot and use those savings on Misiorowski is a job *really* well done in my opinion.\"",
